# Secrets & one-off working files (issue #56)
# A prod superuser password sat in a tracked root script for ten months on a
# public repo. These patterns cover the shapes that let it happen: SQL fragments
# written to the repo root by migration runners, ad-hoc scripts people paste
# credentials into, and database dumps.
temp_migration_*.sql
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
secrets.json
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*-service-role*.json

# Supabase CLI local state (contains pooler connection strings)
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

# logs
*.log
logs/

# builds
build/

app-example
expo-go.apk

# Project documentation and architecture
# NOTE (issue #44): `docs/` used to be listed here while ~60 files under it were
# already tracked — the entry only ever blocked *new* docs from being added,
# which is the opposite of what anyone wanted. Removed so `docs/` is a normal
# tracked directory.
archive/
architecture/

# Audit history (contains historical finding data)
.audit-history/

# Local Netlify folder
.netlify
.commit-automation/cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repo-root sediment (issue #44)
#
# The root had accumulated 62 agent scratch files, 56 one-off investigation
# scripts, 5 compiler/test output dumps and 23 stale session reports — all
# tracked. The point of these patterns is not disk space: it is that nobody
# could tell live code from residue. Keep them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Agent working-directory markers (never belong in the repo)
tmpclaude-*
.claude/worktrees/

# Compiler / test / lint output dumps
ts_errors*.txt
ts_undefined_errors*.txt
ts*-fix-output.txt
tsc_output*.txt
test_output*.txt
lint_output*.txt
*.patch

# One-off investigation scripts written straight into the root.
# Anything worth keeping goes in scripts/ with a header saying what it is for.
/test-*.js
/check-*.js
/debug-*.js
/find-*.js
/search-*.js
/show-*.js
/fix-*.js
/analyze-*.js
/simple-*.js
/temp-*.ts
/repro_*.ts

# BeachRef-app è una repo Flutter separata
BeachRef-app/
